+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## What was done
+`add`, `rename` and `tag` now validate their input before changing anything: a title that is empty or
+blank, or longer than 120 characters once trimmed; a priority other than low/normal/high; a tag that is
+empty or has whitespace. They return an `invalid-input` error whose message says what is wrong. A
+rejected add does not consume an id nor call the clock. Tests added in `test/list.test.ts`.
